name c01m01-werewolves-on-patrol
timeout 600
time 1992-10-29T07:20:00Z

# COMANCHE: MAXIMUM OVERKILL (NovaLogic 1992), CAMPAIGN ONE "OPERATION MAXIMUM OVERKILL",
# MISSION 1 OF 10 -- {Werewolves on Patrol} [MIS].
# Spec, provenance and every open question: mods/comanche/doc/campaign.md, terrain.md,
# substitutions.md, hud.md. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [MIS]: 26 of the 27 objects on map 2 at night -- 14 Werewolves, 4 T-80s and 8 Geckos --
# with the wingman the only thing on the field that is not a goal. "Pick'em off one by one, and let
# your wingman have some fun."
#
# THE FIELD [MIS]: map 2 (Canyonlands, Utah, terrain.md 6), night -- sun -65.08 deg at the lead's
# spawn, computed by the runner. 26 starred objects, unlock marker none - open from the start.
# THE CAST: 14 Werewolf -> `ah64` (11 type-1, 3 type-6) - 4 T-80 -> `target_hard` - 8 Gecko ->
# `sa8` - wingman -> `f16`.
# THE LOADOUT [MIS]: cannon 500, rockets 62, Hellfire 4, Stinger 18, artillery 0, wingman 14, fuel
# 10000. Declared here: 4 x `mk82`, 4 x `aim9`, gun 500, `set fuel_int_pct 50` = 10000 against the
# campaign's own maximum of 20 000. The rockets and the artillery have no row and no mechanism;
# the truncation of the other two is the F-16's nine pylons.

# ---- THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES THAT APPLY TO ALL TEN FILES. Stated in full HERE; the other nine carry
# ---- the short form and point back at this file.
#
# D1  THERE IS NO ROTORCRAFT IN THIS TREE AND NONE WAS INVENTED (CLAUDE.md Prinzip 1). The RAH-66
#     Comanche flies as `module f16`. The error runs against the original in every axis that decides a
#     Comanche mission, and three of the four are MEASURED here rather than asserted:
#       SPEED    the original's simulated top is 177 kt [MAN p.37] and its whole tactic is slower than
#                that. MEASURED: this campaign's pass flown at 180 / 200 / 220 kt CRASHES on the attack
#                egress -- FBPilot's 120 deg turn plus 500 m climb bleeds the jet to 88 kt CAS at 543 m
#                and it mushes into the ground -- and 250 and 275 kt CRASH on mission 2's geometry.
#                300 kt is the LOWEST speed measured to survive every pass tried, so every file here
#                flies 300 kt = 1.70x the original's maximum.
#       HOVER    absent. No collective, no cyclic, no tail-rotor authority, no ground effect, no
#                commanded hover and no auto-hover. The manual builds NoE flight on ground effect
#                [MAN p.18]; nothing in this tree has any of it.
#       HEIGHT   the original is limited to about 500 ft ASL [MAN p.2, 36]. Every file flies its pass at
#                150 m, the game's own ceiling rounded down, and that is the ONE axis where the
#                substitution HELPS: MEASURED on one geometry, the same CCRP delivery misses by
#                26.60 m released from 900 m and by 8.01 m released from 150 m, so a `target_hard` that
#                survives the high pass dies on the low one.
#       AGILITY  not comparable, and not measured: +3 g against +9 g, and yaw is not decoupled from
#                turn anywhere in this tree.
#     Stores map as far as the tree has rows: Hellfire AGM-114 -> `mk82`, Stinger AIM-92 -> `aim9`,
#     20 mm/500 rounds -> `set gun_rounds 500` on the F-16's M61A1. The 500 is the game's own number and
#     it never varies in any of the twenty missions of the 1992 release [MIS].
#
# D2  THE WEREWOLF IS SCENERY, AND THAT IS THIS ROUND'S SHARPEST MEASUREMENT. Ka-50 -> `ah64`, the
#     catalogue's rotorcraft MOVER row. Its kinematics are nearly exact -- 14.63 m span against the
#     Ka-50's 14.5 m rotor, 101.3 m/s max against its published 97 m/s [MAN p.112]. What is absent is
#     the fight: a mover has no combat phase at all. MEASURED across these ten files: 82 Werewolves,
#     ZERO weapon events of any kind. Also measured, separately: an F-16 with `set task intercept`,
#     AIM-9 and AIM-120 against one of them gets ONE RADAR_CONTACT at 3.65 nm and never fires -- a
#     helicopter sits inside every Doppler notch in the tree. And a hand-written Ka-50 catalogue row
#     declared T2 with a 30 mm gun and four stations behaves BYTE-IDENTICALLY to the unarmed
#     `ah64` (`set task bfm` is refused at spawn, "no roll plant"), so an armed rotorcraft is NOT
#     DECLARABLE rather than merely unwritten. REFUSED alternative: `mig17`, which would fight, at the
#     price of putting a 250 kt jet into a title whose subject is 50 m and 100 kt.
#
# D3  THE GROUND IS FLAT AND IT IS NOT THE GAME'S. `--elev const`, 0 m datum, so every altitude in these
#     ten files is ASL and AGL at once. Two structural reasons: (a) nothing in this tree loads the
#     game's own `D*.DTA` heightfields (decoded in terrain.md 1: 1024x1024 bytes at ~1.22 m per unit,
#     0-148 m of total relief); and (b) `mod.json` carries exactly ONE "dem", while this campaign's
#     four maps are anchored to four DISJOINT theatres -- Peru, Utah, Hawaii, Afghanistan
#     (terrain.md 6) -- so no single baked raster can serve them. Consequence: terrain masking, which
#     the manual calls "the essence of modern helicopter warfare" [MAN p.2], does not exist here.
#
# D4  THE CLOCK'S DATE IS [DTA] AND ITS INSTANT IS MEASURED. The date is 1992-10-29, which every file
#     of the 1992 release carries. The UTC instant per mission was chosen and then CHECKED against the
#     runner's own `mission CLOCK` line, which prints the computed sun elevation at the lead's spawn
#     point: the five files campaign.md 2 calls night measure -65.08, -65.11, -83.05, -70.05 and
#     -71.56 deg, the five day files +81.37, +37.89, +44.47, +56.61 and +44.51 deg. No local time is
#     declared anywhere, because no local-time conversion in this reconstruction has provenance.
#
# D5  THE ANCHORING IS A RECONSTRUCTION AND THIS CAMPAIGN NAMES NO PLACE. Ten briefings, zero toponyms
#     [MIS]; all four anchors come from the TRAINING campaign or from morphology, and only map 3's
#     (Kilauea) is named by the game at all (terrain.md 6). Cell -> lat/lon is terrain.md 5's formula
#     with its anchors at cell (512,512) and 10 m per cell -- and the 10 m is itself derived inside a
#     6-14 m bracket (terrain.md 4). If the horizontal scale is wrong, every distance here scales with
#     it.
#
# D6  THE SPAWN HEADING IS NOT THE GAME'S, AND THE REASON IS AN ENGINE FINDING. `set task attack`
#     anchors its run-in leg at the phase's FIRST tick and never corrects a lateral offset, so a striker
#     spawned on the game's own start heading releases across track: MEASURED on this campaign's
#     geometry, aimErrM 249.33 m (mission 1) and 8 382.30 m (mission 3). Every striker here therefore
#     spawns at the game's start CELL on the BEARING to its briefed aim point; the game's heading
#     survives unaltered on every Werewolf and every ground object. The attack phase cannot fly itself
#     onto its own run-in.
#
# D7  ONE STRIKER IS ONE AIM POINT, AND THAT IS WHY EVERY FILE HERE IS RED. `set task attack` releases
#     at the ACTIVE waypoint, flies its egress and hands back to `Route`; nothing in the format and
#     nothing in FBPilot re-enters it, and a `.fbm` has no order source. Blue is the game's own cast --
#     the player, plus the wingman exactly when the loadout's sixth field is non-zero, which is 6 of 10
#     [MIS] -- so at most TWO aim points can be struck per mission against goal sets of 3 to 26. The
#     yield is higher than two wherever the game STACKS objects on one cell (it does, routinely: four
#     T-80s at 230,450 in mission 8, three T-80s and a Gecko at 690,475 in mission 7), and that is the
#     source data's property, not a lucky bomb.
#
# WHAT COULD NOT BE DECLARED AT ALL, each a missing engine capability rather than a missing asset:
#   the 62 unguided 70 mm rockets every mission carries (no rocket store row exists; `hydra70`/`s8` are
#   specified in doc/air-to-ground.md 3.5 and not built) - the artillery calls (five of ten missions
#   carry 2-8 of them; there is no off-map fire support of any kind) - the wingman Hellfire hand-off
#   (no unit may command another unit's release, so the wingman here flies its OWN briefed pass) - the
#   spawn DELAYS (`.fbm` is not a schedule: mission 1's 14-ship stagger over ticks 60-190 and mission
#   6's four reinforcement waves at ticks 3 600-7 200 all spawn at t = 0) - the T-80's "Songster"
#   anti-helicopter missile (a ground target carries no weapon) - and the briefing prose itself.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `lead`'s and nothing else.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires all 26 `kill unit` objectives AND `survive`. It cannot be reached here and
#   the reason is D7, not a tuning failure: two aim points against twenty-six goals.
#   exit 3 = the expected reading. Report the COUNT of met kill objectives; that number is the
#   measurement this file exists to take.
#   exit 1 is what this file actually produces, and it is NOT the lead: `two` carries `survive` alone
#   so that its own loss stays legible, and a dead wingman with a live leader is a damaged flight, not
#   a failed sortie. The game says the same thing from the other side -- the single unstarred object in
#   this mission IS the wingman, so a win with a dead wingman is still a win.
#   exit 2 = an airframe departed controlled flight with nobody having shot it. That is an ENGINE
#   finding, and on this campaign's flight regime it is the finding: see D1's speed sweep.

# MEASURED (exit 1, `--elev const`): FOUR OF TWENTY-SIX, and the exit code is the WINGMAN's.
#   t = 21.3 / 24.6 s   two Mk-82 away, aimErrM 12.64 and 6.53; four Geckos die, because the game
#                       stacks g03+g04 on cell 600,574 and g01+g02 on 744,574
#   t = 118.8 s         `two` takes a 9M33 direct hit (rangeM 0.052, flux 4.94e6) at 997 m -- it was
#                       climbing to its 1 000 m egress waypoint, i.e. OUT of the NoE band the original
#                       never leaves, and the SA-8 that could not reach it at 150 m reached it there
#   verdict             `lead` TIMEOUT, 4 of 26 kill objectives met, `survive` met; `two` FAIL.
#                       24 SA-8 launches, 1 hit.

unit lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight m01 1
  spawn 38.20906 -109.88745 150 159.3 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 50
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 4 mk82
  set store 6 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim9
  set store 8 aim9
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 500
  set cmds_mode auto
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 38.18359 -109.87522 150 300
  wp 38.15115 -109.85964 1000 300
  objective kill unit t01
  objective kill unit t02
  objective kill unit t03
  objective kill unit t04
  objective kill unit g01
  objective kill unit g02
  objective kill unit g03
